WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.760
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and this week
on walking dead we found out what happened

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.280
to the rest of the prison including the remaining
people from the governor’s group.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:21.830
One really big character came back and we
got a huge teaser for their next major destination.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.820
Quick shoutout for my weekly giveaway if you’re
finding me for the first time.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.010
I’ll be selecting one subscriber at random
from the comments to give a twenty dollar

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.150
amazon gift card to.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.410
I’ll announce the winner during my walking
dead Q&amp;A video tomorrow night.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.871
All you have to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment to win.

00:00:36.871 --> 00:00:40.910
But if you want me to include a specific question
in that Q&amp;A, just let me know.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.260
Careful for spoilers from episode 10 if you
haven’t seen it yet, but let’s start with

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.010
our top 5 moments and then I’ll do my review.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.940
Number 5 - Beth and Daryl’s extended camping
trip.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.173
Their whole extended scene was so much fun.

00:00:51.173 --> 00:00:56.059
A lot of comic book readers will remember
that for a brief moment they hooked up, but

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:59.590
since the show messes with a lot of minor
details like that I’m not expecting anything

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:00.590
super sexual to go down between them.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:04.789
Even Daryl’s relationship with Carol got
muted a lot.

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:05.789
Pookie.

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:07.910
Number 4 - Glenn realizes he’s all alone
again.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:12.170
Glenn just loses it and it wasn’t fun to
watch, but it was really intense.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:16.649
I didn’t freak out too much, just because
Glenn always does really well on his own.

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:20.119
I keep remembering that scene from season
1 with him in the charger.

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:25.130
To be fair though, he gets himself into as
many problems as he gets himself out of.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.380
Which is where his better half comes in.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.890
Number 3 - Maggie loses her shit trying to
find glenn.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:34.780
There are so many tumblr gifs of maggie going
crazy and after this episode there will be

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.780
several new ones.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.950
I can only imagine what their children will
end up being like when they grow up someday.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:44.400
I feel like that’s a spoiler for my prediction
that they’ll both survive this season.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.950
If one of them does die though, I think maggie
will be the one.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.229
Lauren Cohan does such an amazing job of selling
anguish and desperation.

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:59.140
They kept trying to fake us out that Glenn
was on the bus, but we saw him in the teaser

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.140
last week.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:05.920
So the moment had already been spoiled.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.890
Number 2 - Abraham’s group to the rescue.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.420
Took them long enough.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.860
We knew they were coming at the end of last
year, but we didn’t know which episode they’d

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.490
debut in or which group would run into them.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.140
I think it’s great that it was Tara.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.740
Obviously Glenn is out cold so he’ll meet
them later.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.030
But this gives Tara the opportunity to start
fresh.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:27.620
She was so hung up on the idea of redemption
and Glenn did an amazing job of explaining

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:39.390
the difference between wants and needs given
the need to find the rest of the survivors.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:45.940
Number 1 - Carol Shows Up with Baby Judith,
Lizzie and Meeka.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:49.920
There were a lot of WTF moments, but Carol
coming back this early and pulling off such

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.440
a big save was my favorite.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.500
I think of Carol’s entrance as like a reverse
Batman.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.070
Like instead of dissapearing when you turn
around, she magically appears.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.710
I love that quick pause she has when she sees
that tyreese has seen her.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:06.280
She doesn’t know whether or not he knows
about Karen.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.569
I’m expecting him to find out soon, but
it seems like for now all will be well between

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:11.740
them.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:17.060
Honorable Mention goes to Lizzie and Mika,
normally I don’t like little kids on intense

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:22.240
drama shows like Walking Dead, but Lizzie
is so hardcore now that watching her try to

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.670
fill Carol’s shoes was really fun.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.370
I feel like a lot of her maturation happened
off screen.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.200
We really only saw her getting yelled at by
Carol and then during the prison plague she

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.260
just kind of tuned everything out and went
dead inside.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:43.709
Cut to the prison attack where she’s gunning
people down without a second though.

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:46.230
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.680
And do you think that Abraham’s group will
go for the sanctuary too?

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.340
Because it seems like everyone else is headed
there.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:58.110
I’m so excited to see what new dynamic Abraham,
rosita and eugene add to the show this season

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.040
and how the rest of the survivors interact
with them.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.860
Right now it’s really just tara and glenn
until they meet up at the sanctuary.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.630
Overall I really liked the episode.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.630
It was another huge shift from the carl-driven
episode last week.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:11.150
I gave that episode an A and I feel like I
have to give this episode at least an A minus.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.021
The only issue in using the entire ensemble
is that you don’t get as many chances to

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.350
develop characters.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.940
Glenn is the exception this time though.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.060
He’s a character that you are really used
to thinking of as a loner, so why wouldn’t

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.880
he show up alone after the prison fight.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.630
I love that he helped Tara out.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.000
I can’t wait to see how she tries to redeem
herself for the rest of the season.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.220
She’s like the new Lizzie of the show now.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.220
Small and helpless but on the path to being
a badass.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.450
I also thought the way the constructed the
story was a lot of fun.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.180
All of the different groups started out from
the same moment in time and things just branched

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.280
from there.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.090
That’s why we kept seeing the same locations
in different times.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.801
Because the character experienced them in
different times.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.330
I want that sign for my room though.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.190
Warning Hitchhikers may be escaping inmates.

